\n- Uses `asyncio.Semaphore` to limit concurrent execution to `max_concurrent` tasks\n- Wraps each task in a semaphore context manager, which ensures proper resource cleanup\n- **Cleanup on interruption:** Even if KeyboardInterrupt happens, each task's `finally` blocks execute because the async context manager releases resources during cancellation\n\n**How it works:**\n1. Creates a semaphore with the max concurrency limit\n2. Wraps each task to acquire the semaphore before running\n3. Runs all tasks concurrently with `asyncio.gather`\n4. If a task is cancelled (via Ctrl+C), its finally block still runs thanks to async context manager semantics\n\nThe tests confirm it respects concurrency limits and that cleanup code runs even during cancellation.","ttft_ms":11156,"type":"result","duration_ms":28694,"uuid":"5f652016-163e-4619-9ae6-1a8c94988cab","ttft_stream_ms":917,"time_to_request_ms":44,"queued_turn_count":0}
